## 724. Find Pivot Index

## Approach 1 — Brute Force
-- Take two variables, "leftSum" and "rightSum".
-- Use an outer loop to consider every index as a possible pivot.
-- Use an inner loop to traverse the array.
-- If j < i, add nums[j] to leftSum.
-- If j > i, add nums[j] to rightSum.
-- After the inner loop, compare leftSum and rightSum.
-- If both are equal, return the current index.
-- If no pivot index is found, return -1.

-- Time Complexity: O(n²)
-- Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int pivotIndex(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int leftSum = 0;
            int rightSum = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (j < i) {
                    leftSum += nums[j];
                }
                if (j > i) {
                    rightSum += nums[j];
                }
            }
            if (leftSum == rightSum) {
                return i;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}

