## Approach 2 — Prefix Sum
-- First calculate the total sum of all elements in the array.
-- Take a variable "leftSum" and initialize it to 0.
-- Traverse the array from left to right.
-- Calculate rightSum using:
   rightSum = totalSum - leftSum - nums[i]
-- If leftSum == rightSum, return the current index.
-- After checking the current index, add nums[i] to leftSum.
-- If no pivot index is found, return -1.

-- Time Complexity: O(n)
-- Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION :
public int pivotIndex(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int totalSum = 0;
        int leftSum = 0;
        // to calculate total sum
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            totalSum += nums[i];
        }

        // leftSum and rightSum
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int rightSum = totalSum - leftSum - nums[i];
            if (leftSum == rightSum)
                return i;
            leftSum += nums[i];
        }
        return -1;
    }
